WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.084
This is Level 2 of the Prompt Studio, on the Claude Pro plan.

00:00:04.084 --> 00:00:05.969
In Level 1 you followed a recipe.

00:00:05.969 --> 00:00:10.710
Here you write your own: define a scenario, craft the prompt, check it, then build.

00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:15.196
On Pro you get more room each session, plus Projects.

00:00:15.196 --> 00:00:21.623
Give each prototype its own Project, and each job its own chat: one for the interview, one to build, one for fixes.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.348
The scenario canvas has twelve parts.

00:00:25.348 --> 00:00:30.676
Each one has a coaching question, examples you can reveal, and live feedback as you type.

00:00:30.676 --> 00:00:32.053
Green means it's clear.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:33.900
Stuck?

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.236
Copy the interview prompt into a new chat.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:39.739
Claude asks you questions one at a time, then writes a summary.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:42.297
Paste the summary here, and press Fill canvas.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.589
Choose a design system, then pick the device, fidelity and output format.

00:00:48.589 --> 00:00:52.720
Tick Ready for Desktop Tester if you'll test your prototype in that app.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:56.210
Press Assemble prompt.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:01:01.133
Your canvas becomes a full prompt in the workspace, and it's yours to edit however you like.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.972
Open the Project kit.

00:01:03.972 --> 00:01:11.850
Copy the Project instructions into your Project, and download scenario.md for its knowledge, so every chat starts already briefed.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:16.661
The quality gate scores your prompt out of ten as you edit.

00:01:16.661 --> 00:01:19.174
Aim for eight before you send a build prompt.

00:01:19.174 --> 00:01:21.687
Then copy it into a new chat in your Project.

00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:27.646
For follow ups, use the prompt patterns, such as three variants or a scope fence.

00:01:27.646 --> 00:01:31.186
And check Fake it honestly for anything that would need a server.

00:01:31.186 --> 00:01:32.003
That's Level 2.
